{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1KI",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So king Solomon was king over all Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the princes which he had; Azariah the son of Zadok the priest,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Elihoreph and Ahiah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehosaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the army: and Zadok and Abiathar ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the priests:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Azariah the son of Nathan ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the officers: and Zabud the son of Nathan ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " principal officer, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the king's friend:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Ahishar ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the household: and Adoniram the son of Abda ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over the tribute.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, who provided victuals for the king and his household: each man his month in a year made provision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their names: The son of Hur, in mount Ephraim:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The son of Dekar, in Makaz, and in Shaalbim, and Beth-shemesh, and Elon-beth-hanan:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The son of Hesed, in Aruboth; to him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pertained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Sochoh, and all the land of Hepher:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The son of Abinadab, in all the region of Dor; who had Taphath the daughter of Solomon for a wife:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Baana the son of Ahilud; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him pertained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Taanach and Megiddo, and all Beth-shean, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by Zartanah beneath Jezreel, from Beth-shean to Abel-meholah, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " beyond Jokneam:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The son of Geber, in Ramoth-gilead; to him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pertained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the towns of Jair the son of Manasseh, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Gilead; to him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also pertained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the region of Argob, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Bashan, sixty great cities with walls and brazen bars:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ahinadab the son of Iddo ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Mahanaim:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ahimaaz ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Naphtali; he also took Basmath the daughter of Solomon for a wife:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Baanah the son of Hushai ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Asher and in Aloth:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shimei the son of Elah, in Benjamin:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Geber the son of Uri ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the country of Gilead, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the country of Sihon king of the Amorites, and of Og king of Bashan; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the only officer who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Judah and Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many, as the sand which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon reigned over all kingdoms from the river to the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt: they brought presents, and served Solomon all the days of his life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon's provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and sixty measures of meal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and a hundred sheep, besides harts, and roebucks, and fallow-deer, and fatted fowls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he had dominion over all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the region",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on this side the river, from Tiphsah even to Azzah, over all the kings on this side of the river: and he had peace on all sides around him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig-tree, from Dan even to Beer-sheba, all the days of Solomon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And those officers provided victuals for king Solomon, and for all that came to king Solomon's table, every man in his month: they lacked nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Barley also and straw for the horses and dromedaries they brought to the place where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the officers",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " were, every man according to his charge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And God gave Solomon great wisdom and understanding, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the sea-shore.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon's wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all the surrounding nations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he spoke three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he spoke of trees, from the cedar tree that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Lebanon even to the hyssop that springeth out of the wall: he spoke also of beasts, and of fowls, and of creeping animals, and of fishes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1KI.4.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1KI.4.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Solomon, from all kings of the earth, who had heard of his wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
